Subject: [PATCH] flash: only animate progress onto a real terminal

The flash progress display is cursor-addressed truecolor redrawn at
30 fps, and it runs whenever a segment exceeds 50 blocks with no check
that stdout is a terminal.

Written to a pipe that is unreadable noise, and at a few hundred KB/s it
can fill the pipe faster than the reader drains it. The client then
blocks in write() and stops servicing the device link, so the flash
stalls with "No ACK from bootloader (timeout)" on a link that is
otherwise healthy.

Gated on g_session.stdoutOnTTY, which the client already computes.

--- a/client/src/flash.c
+++ b/client/src/flash.c
@@ -1027,7 +1027,15 @@
         void (*old_sigint)(int) = SIG_ERR;
         void (*old_sigwinch)(int) = SIG_ERR;
 
-        if (blocks > 50) {
+        // Only animate onto a real terminal. The progress display is
+        // cursor-addressed truecolor redrawn at 30 fps; written to a pipe it
+        // is unreadable noise, and at a few hundred KB/s it can fill the pipe
+        // faster than the reader drains it. The client then blocks in write()
+        // and stops servicing the device, so the flash stalls with "No ACK
+        // from bootloader" on a link that is otherwise fine.
+        bool animate = (blocks > 50) && g_session.stdoutOnTTY;
+
+        if (animate) {
 
             old_sigint = signal(SIGINT, hadouken_on_sigint);
 #ifndef _WIN32
@@ -1045,7 +1053,7 @@
             }
 
             if (write_block(baddr, ctx->ver_info->magic, data, block_size, flash_dev) < 0) {
-                if (blocks > 50) {
+                if (animate) {
                     hadouken_stop();
                     restore_progress_signals(old_sigint, old_sigwinch);
                 }
@@ -1058,13 +1066,13 @@
             length -= block_size;
             block++;
 
-            if (blocks > 50) {
+            if (animate) {
                 pct = (int)(block * 100) / blocks;
                 hadouken_set_progress(pct);
             }
         }
 
-        if (blocks > 50) {
+        if (animate) {
             hadouken_stop();
             restore_progress_signals(old_sigint, old_sigwinch);
         }
